in @prism
in @glass
in @meta
in @spectral
in @uuid/spectral
in @mirror/store
in @mirror/au

# @spectral/gen_prism — the worker primitive.
#
# THE FIRST SUB-SHARD of the @spectral runtime cascade. Lifts the
# 2026-05-11 informal naming in `boot/std/spectral/portal.mirror`
# (where `gen_prism` was first used as a substrate keyword) and the
# 2026-06-01 boot-altitude declaration at
# `boot/std/mirror/runtime/gen_prism.mirror` (where `type gen_prism`
# carried the autopoietic self-reference shape) to the substrate
# altitude under the @spectral family root.
#
# Per docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §2 (2026-06-10, Mara): gen_prism
# is the substrate's `gen_server` analogue (BEAM/OTP). A gen_prism
# carries three surfaces — identity, state, tool surface — and a
# lifecycle contract owned by its parent supervisor. The five-op
# block IS the tool surface (the wire protocol); external callers
# (other gen_prisms, the supervisor, MCP-mounted readers) speak to
# a gen_prism through its five-op surface. There is no out-of-band
# API.
#
# === The keyword decision ===
#
# `glass` per recognition #46 (path-syntax property; promoted) and
# `shards/spectral.mirror`'s discipline section: "@spectral
# sub-shards at depth >= 1 use `glass`; the family root itself uses
# `prism` per the depth-0 discipline."
#
# Why NOT a new substrate keyword (like the eight optical schematic
# keywords declared in `shards/optics.mirror` at tick 6443e6e):
# the optical keywords declared NEW STRUCTURAL KINDS (facet, stage,
# aperture, splitter, resonator, bench, source, detector) — each
# names a passive composition primitive of physical optics. The
# gen_prism is NOT a new structural kind; it IS a sub-prism
# specialisation (the BEAM gen_server analogue), which is exactly
# what `glass` declares (per `shards/glass.mirror`'s `glass(name)
# -> prism` form). Adding a `gen_prism` keyword would proliferate
# discriminators that the substrate's existing `glass` keyword
# already covers.
#
# The relationship to the optical keywords (per recognition #58
# PROMOTED): a `gen_prism` spawned inside a `bench` IS one of the
# optical elements (source / facet / detector / etc.) at runtime —
# its five-op tool surface IS the element's apertures; its
# start/restart/terminate lifecycle IS the resonator round-trip.
# The optical keyword names what the element IS structurally (at
# declaration time); `gen_prism` names what it IS operationally
# (at runtime). NOT competing keywords; SAME substrate-altitude
# object viewed from different sides.
#
# === Identity — uuid_spectral ===
#
# Per docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §2 and
# `shards/uuid/spectral.mirror`:
#
#   - the ACTIVE 48 bits (quantized SpectralCoordinate<5>) place the
#     gen_prism in the substrate's spectral manifold for routing
#     (Fate's mycelial routing reads through this);
#   - the DARK 80 bits identify the process for entanglement, parent
#     edges, and registry lookup (BLAKE3-truncated content hash).
#
# The autopoietic claim from
# `boot/std/mirror/runtime/gen_prism.mirror`'s `name:
# zoom(oid, gen_prism)` fixed-point construction lifts here through
# `uuid_spectral`'s content-addressed identity surface: the
# gen_prism's identity IS the content address of its own declaration
# under itself, expressed at the spectral altitude via
# `uuid_spectral`'s dark portion. The Banach contraction on hash
# space (Soto-Andrade & Varela 1984) guarantees the fixed point.
#
# === State surface — shard_ref ===
#
# Per docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §2 and
# `shards/mirror/store.mirror`: the gen_prism's observable state IS
# the shard's content. State changes IS a settle into a new shard
# (uuid_spectral-addressed; the lattice ascent per
# [[architecture-shard-as-crdt]]). The runtime NEVER carries opaque
# in-memory state outside the shard; every observable transition is
# store-visible.
#
# `shard_ref` (declared at `@mirror/store`) is the typed handle:
# `type shard_ref = uuid_spectral`. The gen_prism's `state` field
# carries a `shard_ref`; resolution to the underlying shard happens
# through `@mirror/store.read`.
#
# === Tool surface — the five-op block ===
#
# Per docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §2 (the runtime-altitude
# reading of the five operations):
#
#   focus    λ₀ projection: what is this gen_prism's ground-state
#            shard? (the canonical observable state)
#   project  which subspace of the state surface is observable to
#            the caller? (caller-relative projection of the shard)
#   split    orthogonal decomposition of current state across child
#            gen_prisms (the supervisor's `split` IS its registry
#            walk)
#   shift    basis transformation: same content, different altitude
#            (e.g. an @io boundary view of a @facet/rust state shard)
#   settle   measurement collapse: drive any pending `au` into a new
#            shard through the property chain; the state surface
#            advances by one lattice element
#
# The five operations at runtime altitude collapse to the same
# algebra `prism` carries at every altitude (per
# [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]]); the runtime
# reading is the operational interpretation per
# [[architecture-operations-as-linear-algebra]].
#
# === Lifecycle — start / terminate / restart ===
#
# Per docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §3: every gen_prism has
# exactly one parent. The parent edge is the lifecycle edge: the
# parent owns the child's birth, restart, and death. The
# parent-edge class is acyclic across the substrate. The root
# supervisor (parentless) is the vocabulary anchor at ~/.mirror/.
#
# `start(parent: gen_prism) -> gen_prism` — the parent's request
# to spawn a child; the child's parent edge is set at this call.
# `terminate() -> au` — the gen_prism's exit; produces an `au`
# (proposed-but-not-yet-settled state per `@mirror/au`) carrying
# the final state delta; the supervisor settles it into the
# parent's registry shard.
# `restart() -> gen_prism` — supervisor-initiated re-spawn; the
# new gen_prism shares identity (same uuid_spectral) but advances
# the tick counter on its lifecycle ledger.
#
# Per docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §3: the supervisor's
# restart-strategy contract is a kintsugi morphism. When a child
# fails, the restart decision is the substrate-pull-correct
# transformation under the supervision invariant. The bodies
# discharge through @kintsugi at the supervisor altitude
# (forward-promised; `shards/spectral/supervisor.mirror`).
#
# === Recursion: gen_prism is closed under composition ===
#
# Per docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §2: a gen_prism is recursive.
# Its state surface MAY itself be a supervisor's registry shard,
# and the gen_prism IS a supervisor. The vocabulary is the same at
# every depth; the algebra is closed. `supervisor` (forward-promised
# at `shards/spectral/supervisor.mirror`) is a gen_prism
# specialisation; same surface, restart-strategy invariant on the
# registry shard.
#
# === Cascade siblings (forward-promised, NOT landing this tick) ===
#
#   shards/spectral/supervisor.mirror     gen_prism specialisation;
#                                          child_spec, restart strategy,
#                                          registry contract
#   shards/spectral/parent.mirror         single-parent lifecycle edge
#                                          type (acyclic)
#   shards/spectral/entanglement.mirror   peer correlation edge; sheaf
#                                          restriction map at substrate
#                                          altitude
#   shards/spectral/registry.mirror       supervisor's child registry;
#                                          query surface
#   shards/spectral/root.mirror           parentless supervisor;
#                                          vocabulary anchor at
#                                          ~/.mirror/
#   shards/spectral/portal.mirror         runtime side of portal
#                                          (gen_prism specialisation
#                                          carrying the frame stream)
#
# This tick lands the FLOOR (gen_prism); siblings land as the
# cascade pulls each one (per the substrate-pull discipline:
# property surfaces opacity, the next consumer pulls the closure).
#
# === Honest partial discipline (per #306) ===
#
# The action bodies below all carry `\` obligation blocks — no
# fracture body emits any morphism in this tick. No `partials`
# declaration needed (per `dissonance_partials_match_ast_breadth`
# #306). Bodies discharge downstream when the consumer pulls
# realisation through `@facet/metalogue/materialize` (per the
# ouroboros pipeline in docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §5).
#
# Spec context: docs/math/the-tower/beam-runtime.md §2.2 (actors as
#               sections of a principal bundle; the gen_prism carrier
#               below IS the substrate-altitude section at BEAM/process
#               altitude; identity=uuid_spectral autopoietic fixed
#               point per Lawvere; state=shard_ref settles lattice
#               ascent; parent=uuid_spectral parallel-transport base;
#               Mara `610c6d6`);
#               docs/specs/gen-prism-as-bundle-section-and-dance-as-
#               ensemble-connection.md §2.1 (canonical spec naming
#               gen_prism as bundle section; Mara `fee2727`);
#               docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md (the ouroboros
#               spec; §2 gen_prism shape; §3 supervision tree;
#               §8 cascade map).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-three-tier-stack]] (the
#                      SpectralSupervisor precedent),
#                      [[architecture-hamilton-scheduler]] (the
#                      per-shard memory manager; gen_prism is the
#                      shard-supervised worker),
#                      [[architecture-shard-as-crdt]] (the state
#                      surface IS a shard; state changes ARE
#                      lattice ascent),
#                      [[architecture-operations-as-linear-algebra]]
#                      (the runtime reading of the five ops),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                      (the gen_prism name lived in
#                      boot/std/spectral/portal.mirror since
#                      2026-05-11; this tick names the parent at the
#                      substrate altitude).
# Related shards: spectral.mirror (the family root this glass is
#                  under),
#                 uuid/spectral.mirror (the identity carrier;
#                  uuid_spectral active+dark structure),
#                 mirror/store.mirror (the state-surface carrier;
#                  shard_ref = uuid_spectral),
#                 mirror/au.mirror (the proposed-shard carrier;
#                  terminate's return shape),
#                 mirror/spectral/portal.mirror (the form-side
#                  declaration of portal-as-gen_prism per the
#                  26th-instance recognition),
#                 optics.mirror (the schematic-altitude vocabulary
#                  a gen_prism instantiates when spawned inside a
#                  bench per recognition #58).
# Realisation reference: boot/std/mirror/runtime/gen_prism.mirror
#                  (the boot-floor declaration; this shard lifts
#                  the substrate-altitude reading; the boot floor
#                  is retained as a transitional placeholder during
#                  consumer-pull migration through
#                  @facet/metalogue/materialize).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/spectral/gen_prism.mirror` declares
# `@spectral/gen_prism` and only that.

glass @spectral/gen_prism {
  focus gen_prism
  project gen_prism
  split gen_prism
  shift gen_prism
  settle gen_prism
}

# === gen_prism — the worker record ===
#
# Three surfaces:
#   identity — `uuid_spectral`; both halves load-bearing (active 48
#              bits for routing; dark 80 bits for parentage,
#              entanglement, registry lookup);
#   state    — `shard_ref`; the gen_prism's observable state
#              resolves through @mirror/store.read; state changes
#              ARE settles into a new shard (the lattice ascent);
#   parent   — `uuid_spectral`; the lifecycle owner. Every gen_prism
#              has exactly one parent; the parent edge is acyclic
#              at this edge class (per
#              docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §3). The root
#              supervisor's parent field IS its own identity (the
#              parentless top of the supervision tree).
#
# The tool surface (the five-op block above) is NOT a record field;
# it IS the wire protocol the type exposes by virtue of being a
# `glass @spectral/gen_prism` declaration. Per
# [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]]: a glass declaration
# IS the trait the carrier implements; the five operations are
# accessible on any value of this type.
type gen_prism = {
  identity: uuid_spectral,
  state:    shard_ref,
  parent:   uuid_spectral,
}

# === start — supervisor-initiated spawn ===
#
# The parent's request to spawn a child gen_prism. The child's
# parent edge is set at this call (per
# docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §3). The returned `gen_prism`
# carries a fresh identity derived from the autopoietic fixed
# point on the parent's registry shard plus the initial state
# shard.
#
# Per the BEAM analogue: this is `Supervisor.start_child/2`. The
# supervisor's restart-strategy invariant gates which children
# may be started; the body discharges downstream at
# `shards/spectral/supervisor.mirror`.
start(parent: gen_prism) -> gen_prism { \ }

# === terminate — exit, return final delta as au ===
#
# The gen_prism's exit. Produces an `au` (proposed-but-not-yet-
# settled state per `@mirror/au`) carrying the final state delta.
# The supervisor settles the `au` into the parent's registry shard
# (lattice ascent); the registry's view of the child transitions
# from `running` to `terminated` content-addressed at the new
# registry shard.
#
# Per docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §3: terminate is one of the
# three lifecycle events the parent owns (start / restart /
# terminate). The `au` return is the substrate's invariant: every
# observable transition produces a settle-able proposed shard;
# nothing is lost into opaque in-memory state.
terminate() -> au { \ }

# === restart — supervisor-initiated re-spawn ===
#
# The supervisor's restart decision (the kintsugi morphism per
# docs/specs/spectral-runtime.md §3) re-spawns the gen_prism. The
# new gen_prism shares identity (same `uuid_spectral`) — the
# autopoietic fixed point on hash space is invariant under
# restart — but advances the tick counter on its lifecycle ledger
# (recorded in the parent's registry shard).
#
# Per the BEAM analogue: this is the supervisor's automatic
# restart-on-failure path. The body discharges through @kintsugi
# at the supervisor altitude (the restart decision IS a kintsugi
# morphism evaluated at the supervisor's eigenboard context
# slice).
restart() -> gen_prism { \ }

out @spectral/gen_prism
out gen_prism
out start
out terminate
out restart
